SUMMARY:Deadline 12:00 Hong Kong time: Hong Kong PhD Fellowship Scheme 2027
 /28 (HKD 344\,400 a year for up to three years\; 400 fellowships\, practic
 e-led art PhDs included)
DESCRIPTION:Closes 01 Dec 2026 at 12:00 Hong Kong time.\n\nThe Hong Kong Ph
 D Fellowship Scheme\, run by the Research Grants Council\, funds around 40
 0 new full-time PhD students a year at eight Hong Kong universities\, in a
 ny discipline\, including AI\, computing and data science programmes and p
 ractice-led art research (Hong Kong Baptist University's Academy of Visual
  Arts promotes the scheme for practice-led and practice-based PhDs with ac
 cess to its...\n\nOrganisation: Research Grants Council (RGC) of Hong Kong
 \, with eight Hong Kong universities\nLocation: Hong Kong: City University
  of Hong Kong\, Hong Kong Baptist University\, Lingnan University\, The Ch
 inese University of Hong Kong\, The Education University of Hong Kong\, Th
 e Hong Kong Polytechnic University\, HKUST and The University of Hong Kong
 . Open to applicants of any country of origin.\nAward: Annual stipend of H
 KD 344\,400 (about USD 44\,150) plus a conference and research travel allo
 wance of HKD 14\,400 a year\, for up to three years (2026/27 rates as publ
 ished by the RGC). Some universities add top-ups: HKBU lists a HKD 40\,000
 -a-year Elite Scholar Award for three years\, a further HKD 20\,000 travel
  top-up\, four years of tuition waiver and two years of guaranteed accommo
 dation. 400 fellowships for 2027/28.\nDuration: Full-time PhD\, up to thre
 e years of fellowship funding (HKBU programmes run four years).\n\nMore: h
 ttps://cerg1.ugc.edu.hk/hkpfs/index.html?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrant
 desk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://cerg1.ugc.edu.hk/hkpfs/index.html?utm_source=artificialnouveaug
 rantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Hong Kong: City University of Hong Kong\, Hong Kong Baptist Univer
 sity\, Lingnan University\, The Chinese University of Hong Kong\, The Educ
 ation University of Hong Kong\, The Hong Kong Polytechnic University\, HKU
 ST and The University of Hong Kong. Open to applicants of any country of o
 rigin.
END:VEVENT
